WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.377
Hi, I'm Pimpernel!

00:00:02.377 --> 00:00:03.826
Attention keeps every token.

00:00:03.826 --> 00:00:07.450
Mamba keeps one small state, and chooses what goes in.

00:00:09.017 --> 00:00:12.664
The idea: each token sets its own step size and projections, so

00:00:12.664 --> 00:00:14.487
the state chooses what to keep.

00:00:19.358 --> 00:00:20.622
One step, one channel.

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:22.861
The exponential decays the state.

00:00:22.861 --> 00:00:25.867
A small step keeps it; a large one wipes it.

00:00:26.287 --> 00:00:28.122
Delta times B writes the token in.

00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:30.764
C reads it out.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:32.587
All three come from the token itself.

00:00:34.358 --> 00:00:38.291
S4 fixed them per layer, so it unrolled into one long

00:00:38.291 --> 00:00:39.722
convolution, blind to content.

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:41.579
Selection breaks the convolution.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:44.813
Mamba runs a scan instead, and can skip filler.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.282
Only the small inputs sit in slow memory.

00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:54.035
They're loaded once into fast on-chip memory, where each step's decay is computed.

00:00:54.738 --> 00:00:57.456
The scan runs there, never writing the big state out.

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:01.364
Only the outputs go back.

00:01:01.364 --> 00:01:02.793
Backward recomputes the states.

00:01:04.458 --> 00:01:07.609
Mamba-2 makes the decay one number per head.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:12.334
Then the layer is one masked matrix, attention without softmax, computed in

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:13.910
chunks of matrix multiplies.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.708
At two thousand tokens, a Transformer's cache is over six hundred megabytes.

00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:22.280
Mamba's state is about twelve, and fixed.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.227
But a fixed state can't copy a long document back.

00:01:27.227 --> 00:01:30.287
So hybrids keep some attention: one layer in four, here.

00:01:30.707 --> 00:01:32.756
Only those layers keep a cache that grows.

00:01:35.058 --> 00:01:37.592
A selective state decides what to remember.

00:01:37.592 --> 00:01:40.488
A few attention layers recall the rest exactly.

00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:45.301
Selection from each token.

00:01:45.301 --> 00:01:47.528
A scan, then chunked matrix multiplies.

00:01:47.528 --> 00:01:50.125
A fixed state, with a little attention.

00:01:50.545 --> 00:01:52.744
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:52.744 --> 00:01:53.373
I'm Pimpernel.

00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:53.687
Bye!
